#
# Conformance case: enactment/frontier-roster-derives-every-label
#
# The CLOSED next-action frontier, argued in full. `frontier-labels-are-derived`
# shows that a label CAN be derived; this case shows that EVERY label is. Not one
# logic:entryLabel appears in the data world, and all SIXTEEN logic:FrontierLabel
# individuals come out of the sixteen logic:Rule instances profile.json names in
# "shipped_rules", resolved by IRI out of slices/grounding/logic/module.ttl, so the
# case reasons with the rules that actually ship rather than a restatement of them.
#
# A roster that enumerates sixteen positions and can compute five of them is the
# named required-negative of the enactment kernel: an incomplete frontier presented
# as closed. Sixteen entries, sixteen derived labels, zero asserted ones is what
# retires it.
#
#   preconditionBlockedEntry      StepPending
#                                   -> FrontierBlockedPrecondition
#   readyAuthorizedEntry          StepReady + ApprovalNull
#                                   -> FrontierReadyAuthorized
#   approvalRequiredEntry         StepReady + ApprovalCreated
#                                   -> FrontierReadyApprovalRequired
#   capabilityBlockedEntry        StepWaiting + a gap on its action step
#                                   -> FrontierBlockedCapabilityOrResource
#   awaitingInputEntry            StepWaiting + entryAwaits
#                                   -> FrontierWaitingOnEventTimeOrInput
#   excludedEntry                 entryExcludes another entry
#                                   -> FrontierMutuallyExclusive
#   reconciliationRequiredEntry   EffectAttempted
#                                   -> FrontierReconciliationRequired
#   compensationEligibleEntry     EffectReceipted
#                                   -> FrontierCompensationEligible
#   compensationRequiredEntry     EffectReconciled + InfoSupported + EnactmentFailed
#                                   -> FrontierCompensationRequired
#   compensationFailedEntry       StepFailed + EffectCompensating + InfoSupported
#                                 + EnactmentRunning
#                                   -> FrontierCompensationFailedForwardCommitted
#   reconciliationForeclosedEntry EffectAbandoned
#                                   -> FrontierReconciliationImpossible
#   completedEntry                StepCompleted
#                                   -> FrontierCompleted
#   skippedEntry                  StepSkipped + skipReason
#                                   -> FrontierSkippedWithTypedReason
#   cancelledEntry                StepCancelled + EnactmentCancelled
#                                 + InfoNotEvaluated
#                                   -> FrontierCancelled
#   cancelledInFlightEntry        StepCancelled + EnactmentCancelled
#                                 + InfoUndetermined
#                                   -> FrontierCancelledWithInFlightEffects
#   terminallyFailedEntry         StepFailed + EnactmentFailed
#                                   -> FrontierTerminallyFailed
#
# Four pairs carry the disjointness argument, and each pair differs on exactly one
# axis. readyAuthorizedEntry and approvalRequiredEntry differ on the approval axis;
# cancelledEntry and cancelledInFlightEntry on the commitment-knowledge axis;
# terminallyFailedEntry and compensationFailedEntry on the enactment axis;
# capabilityBlockedEntry and awaitingInputEntry share the waiting position and are
# told apart by what is recorded about the obstruction — a step blocked by a
# capability the deployment does not have awaits nothing, because what is absent
# does not arrive.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix e:     <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformance/frontier-roster/> .

# --- The data world: sixteen entries, and NOT ONE logic:entryLabel -------------
#
# The sixteen rules are not restated here. profile.json's "shipped_rules" names
# them, and the harness resolves each IRI against slices/grounding/logic/module.ttl,
# hard-failing on one the module no longer declares. A copy inside this file would
# keep the case green after the shipped rule was deleted — the roster would then
# certify the completeness of its own copy, which is the very failure this case is
# the required-negative for.

e:preconditionBlockedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepPending .

e:readyAuthorizedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepReady, logic:ApprovalNull .

e:approvalRequiredEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepReady, logic:ApprovalCreated .

# Waiting on a capability the deployment does not have. The gap on its action step
# is the discriminator; waiting alone reaches no label.
e:capabilityBlockedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAction e:ocrStep ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepWaiting .

e:ocrStep a logic:TransactionStep .
e:ocrGap a logic:OperationalCapabilityGap ;
    logic:gapBlockedStep e:ocrStep .

# The same waiting position, told apart by what is recorded about the obstruction:
# this one NAMES what it awaits, and what is absent does not arrive.
e:awaitingInputEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAwaits e:scannerCallback ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepWaiting .


# Exclusivity is a relation between two candidates and belongs on no axis at all.
e:excludedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryExcludes e:readyAuthorizedEntry .

e:reconciliationRequiredEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:EffectAttempted .

e:compensationEligibleEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:EffectReceipted .

e:compensationRequiredEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:EffectReconciled, logic:InfoSupported,
                           logic:EnactmentFailed .

# The enactment axis is the discriminator against terminallyFailedEntry: the run is
# still going because escalation remains open.
e:compensationFailedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepFailed, logic:EffectCompensating,
                           logic:InfoSupported, logic:EnactmentRunning .

e:reconciliationForeclosedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:EffectAbandoned .

e:completedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepCompleted .

# A skip refuses to reach its label without a TYPED reason, because an untyped skip
# is indistinguishable from an oversight.
e:skippedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepSkipped ;
    logic:skipReason logic:SkipAlreadySatisfied .

e:cancelledEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepCancelled, logic:EnactmentCancelled,
                           logic:InfoNotEvaluated .

# One axis apart from cancelledEntry — the commitment-knowledge axis — and a wholly
# different instruction: effects may already have committed outside the system.
e:cancelledInFlightEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepCancelled, logic:EnactmentCancelled,
                           logic:InfoUndetermined .

e:terminallyFailedEntry a logic:FrontierEntry ;
    logic:entryAxisWitness logic:StepFailed, logic:EnactmentFailed .
